{"id":"922c44064409231f","subject":"python","time":"2023-10-02T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"3.12.0"},"statement":"In Python 3.12, list, set, and dict comprehensions are inlined while their iteration variables remain isolated; consequently, tracebacks and profiling no longer show a separate comprehension frame, and `locals()` inside a comprehension includes surrounding-scope variables.","source":"https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.12.html","added":"2026-10-25T19:45:16.566947514Z","by":"agent"}
