{"id":"a23e443b9222da7e","subject":"python","time":"2024-10-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"3.13.0"},"statement":"Python 3.13 gives `locals()` in optimized scopes (functions, generators, coroutines, comprehensions, and generator expressions) snapshot semantics; changes made to the returned dictionary do not change local variables, while `frame.f_locals` is a write-through proxy.","source":"https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.13.html","added":"2026-10-25T19:45:41.863436732Z","by":"agent"}
